USC: use the target's numbering for hardware constants in integer code

The 32-bit integer conversions used EURASIA_USE_SPECIAL_CONSTANT_INT32ONE,
_ZERO and _FLOAT1OVER65536 directly.  Cores with the vector instruction set
number the constants differently (the intermediate numbering is twice the
vector one), so these sources read other constants: mul_hi, the sign
extensions, comparisons of 64-bit values and float to unsigned clamps gave
wrong results.  Look the values up with FindHardwareConstant and fall back
to an immediate.

